WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.002
 Brent, Thomas,
congratulations.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.070
You've made it into the
third and final round

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:06.405
of this competition.

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.975
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:12.812
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history--

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:16.649
[tense music]

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.451
The Tizona del Cid.

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:20.553
 Oh, my.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.154
 What is that?

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:25.759
 Looking at the blade,
I see this super ornate

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.193
guard and pommel.

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:31.698 line:0%
And I'm thinking, how can I
get all this in detail into it

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:34.968 line:0%
and make it strong
and functional?

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:35.968
 Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.236
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.037
 Good luck, brother.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.472
 Good luck.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:43.176 line:7%
[music playing]

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:46.312
 Today I have to
make El Cid's Telzona.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.914
I'm getting the tang,
drawn out but I noticed

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.217
the tang is getting twisted.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.085
And I'm really
worried at this point

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:55.622
because this could
cause a lot of stress.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:58.124
I will definitely have a little
catching up to do tomorrow.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.627 line:7%
[heavy metal music]

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:01.861
 We're here in West Virginia.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.429
Let's get these
burners a burning.

00:01:03.495 --> 00:01:06.465 line:0%
El Cid' blade is a
very light blade.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:10.503
I'm really concerned about how
I'm going to keep it that way.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.271
After a few hours of
forging, I finally

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.840
had my piece at the length.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.474
I climb up on the
little steppy stool,

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:19.979
and I could barely get the tip
of this blade into the quench.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.347
The quench went all right.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:25.184 line:0%
Tomorrow I have to move
on to the pretty stuff.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:29.022 line:0%
 It's day two, and I
am going to start over.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:30.056
It's pedal to the metal.

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:31.323
I've gotta hurry.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.525
I absolutely need to
quench this plate tonight,

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:36.695
or I am going to be
drastically behind.

00:01:36.762 --> 00:01:40.600
So I've got my blade forged
out to the shape I want.

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:42.802
I'm leaving my tank
bigger than I need so

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:46.171
that, as I'm holding this
gigantic, long piece,

00:01:46.238 --> 00:01:48.107
it doesn't bend at the tang.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:52.177
[heavy metal music]

00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:55.815
Today I got my blade
forged and quenched.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:56.616
So happy.

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:01.387 line:0%
 Today's main goal was
to get the guard assembly.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.123
There's a lot of artistic
work involved with this piece.

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:05.357
 This is the kind
of work I'm really

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.193
used to, these
little, small twists

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:10.163
and bends, basic blacksmithing.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:11.497
So I've got all my welding done.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:14.767
Now it's time to clean this
thing up on the grinder.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.168
 That is beautiful.

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:17.803 line:7%
I love that.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.071 line:0%
 Right now, I've
got the majority

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:20.840 line:7%
of my guard constructed.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:25.311
I have to add a little crossbar
to weld on as a cross-guard.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.847
For the pommel, I plan on just
cutting a little cone out.

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:30.082
I got it nice and sharp.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:32.251
My thin finish
isn't perfect, but I

00:02:32.317 --> 00:02:34.120
made this sword in three days.

00:02:34.186 --> 00:02:36.222
So even if you feel
like you can't do it,

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.490
just give it a shot.

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.459
You really never know
what's going to happen.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:40.760 line:7%
[music playing]

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.096 line:0%
 Here we are, the
last day of this build.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:44.831
Everything has
progressed nicely so far.

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:48.067
Now I'm going to start the
mustard petina process.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.702
Basically, the vinegar
and the mustard

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:50.870
reacts to high-carbon steel.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.905
The blade begins to slightly
rust and wipe it off,

00:02:52.971 --> 00:02:55.507
and you have a nice, little
outline where you mustard was.

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:56.375
 All right.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.978
I'm very, very, very
happy with that.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.246
That is wild.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:01.814
 Before I see this
blade off, I've

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.782
just got to test it one time.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:07.453
And the blade just passes
right through like hot butter.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.121
Eat your heart out, El Cid.

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:11.156
 We got it done.

00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:12.124
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:14.494
Welcome to the keel test.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.996
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapons will do,

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.297
I will take your
weapon and deliver

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.399
some slashes and thrusts
on this boar carcass.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.401
Brent, you are first.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.468
Are you ready for this?

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:23.403
 Yeah.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.570
Let's do it so my knees
will stop shaking.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.137
 All right.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.139
Let's do this.

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:32.412
[heavy metal music]

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:35.815
 Wow.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:52.498
 Good job.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:53.299
 Wow.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.104
 All right, Brent.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.471
Let's talk about
your Tizona here.

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:01.107
The balance of this
blade allows me

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:05.945
to really move around with it,
and it's a very sharp edge.

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:08.781
Overall this weapon is one
that you can move and bring

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.784
to combat, and it will kill.

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:13.085
 Thank you, sir.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.086
 Good job.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.020
 All right, Thomas.
Your turn.

00:04:15.087 --> 00:04:15.888
You ready?

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:16.889
 Ready as I'll ever be.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:17.656
 All right.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.424
Let's do this.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:23.630
[heavy metal music]

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.380
 Nice.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.854
 Your tip thrusts easy
and cuts on the way out.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.824
And your edge-- as you can
see, same number of cuts

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:53.259
cut all the way through.

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:56.028
Your first sword-- it will kill.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:56.795
Good job.

00:04:56.862 --> 00:04:57.864
 Thank you.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.599
 It's OK to be thrilled, kid.

00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:01.867
 [laughs] Is it?

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.504
[tense music]

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:05.771
 All right, gentlemen.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.508
It's time for the strength
test, the armor chop.

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.843
To test the strength and overall
construction of your blades,

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:14.113
I'll be chopping into
our armored knights here.

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:14.947
Brent, you're up first.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:15.714
You ready?

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:16.982
 Yes, sir.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:20.987
[heavy metal music]

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:36.268
 All right, Brent.

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:38.537
You've got a couple
of chips and rolls.

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:42.308
I don't know that it'll affect
the performance of your blade.

00:05:42.374 --> 00:05:43.575
It's still sharp.

00:05:43.642 --> 00:05:45.477
As far as the design
of your blade,

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:47.713
that's a very slick handle.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:51.350
I'd like to not be able
to do that as easily.

00:05:51.416 --> 00:05:52.318
But you did good.

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:54.253
It's a strong sword, one piece.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:54.987
Good job.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.522
 Thank you.

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.724
 Tomas, are you ready?

00:05:58.791 --> 00:05:59.291
 I'm ready.

00:05:59.324 --> 00:06:00.392
Swing away.

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:04.564
[heavy metal music]

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:18.311
 All right.

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:21.381
Thomas, this has a
really fine edge to it.

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:25.784
And where it made contact,
there are multiple rolls.

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:28.387
That's that superfine
edge just being pushed

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.990
over as it hits that armor.

00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:34.293
It's an amazingly light
sword for as wide as that is.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:35.494
That's very good work.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.930
I mean, it's a very
broad blade, and it's

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.899
got a very light feel to it.

00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:43.436
The handle on this, the wrapping
on there gives a good grip.

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:45.737
It felt really good in my hand.

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:47.472
Bottom line-- it's
a strong sword.

00:06:47.539 --> 00:06:49.108
It held up beautifully.

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:49.875
Good job.

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:50.676
 Thank you.

00:06:55.147 --> 00:06:56.348
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:06:56.415 --> 00:06:58.884
This is the sharpness
test, the fish slice.

00:06:58.917 --> 00:07:01.086
To test the edge of
your weapon, I will

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:03.222
slash away at these salmons.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:04.190
Brent, you are first.

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:04.924
Are you ready?

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:05.491
 Let's do it.

00:07:05.525 --> 00:07:07.226
 Let's do it.

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:11.831
[tense music]

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:20.173
[heavy metal music]

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:34.053
 Wow.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.054
 Good job.

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:38.457
 All right.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:39.859
Let's talk about
your sword here.

00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:42.295
It cut all the way through
the fishes except for that.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.395
It's a sharp edge.

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:45.164
All the cuts here
are very clean.

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:47.433
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.167
 Awesome.

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:49.201
Thank you.

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:51.170
 All right, Thomas.

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:52.404
Ready for sushi?

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:53.439
 I am ready.

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:54.974
 Let's do this.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.209
 It's really down to
the wire at this point.

00:07:57.276 --> 00:08:01.980
If my blade doesn't perform as
well as Brent's, I'm definitely

00:08:02.047 --> 00:08:05.217
out of this competition.

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:09.255
[heavy metal music]

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:27.439
 Wow.

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:28.440
Good job.

00:08:28.473 --> 00:08:29.642
 Heck yeah.

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:33.979
 All right, Thomas.

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:37.049
Every cut was clean
all the way through.

00:08:37.115 --> 00:08:39.217
Once again, the edge here
despite some of the rolls

00:08:39.284 --> 00:08:43.088
it took earlier, had no issues
in performance and quality

00:08:43.155 --> 00:08:43.789
of cuts.

00:08:43.856 --> 00:08:46.458
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:08:46.525 --> 00:08:47.592
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:08:47.659 --> 00:08:53.332
The new Forged in Fire
champion is Brent.

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:54.466
Congratulations.

00:08:54.533 --> 00:08:56.001
You're the new Forged
in Fire champion.

00:08:56.068 --> 00:09:00.506
Thomas, unfortunately, a
setback in your home forge

00:09:00.572 --> 00:09:03.309
cost you a little
bit of detail when

00:09:03.375 --> 00:09:04.910
it came to your final product.

00:09:04.976 --> 00:09:07.580
And for that reason,
please leave the forge.

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:08.980
[music playing]

00:09:09.047 --> 00:09:11.183
 I'm super disappointed
that I didn't win,

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.751
but I came out here.

00:09:12.784 --> 00:09:14.486
I made a knife with a drum set.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:17.022
I made a sword for
the first time.

00:09:17.056 --> 00:09:19.659
I'm just so proud
of myself for having

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:23.763
taken the risk, putting myself
outside of my comfort zone.

00:09:23.796 --> 00:09:26.632
And right now, I feel
like a rock star.

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:29.835
 Brent, congratulations.

00:09:29.901 --> 00:09:31.437
You are the Forged
in Fire champion,

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.640
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:34.707 --> 00:09:35.474
Good job, my friend.

00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:37.109
[applause]

00:09:37.176 --> 00:09:38.344
 Oh, it feels amazing.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.180
The adrenaline right now is
just through the friggin roof.

00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:43.382
I'd like to thank God
for this opportunity,

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:47.286
my wife for her support.

00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:48.554
Just thank you, everyone.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.722
I have trouble
containing everything.

00:09:50.789 --> 00:09:53.392
There's so many emotions
inside right now that I

00:09:53.425 --> 00:09:54.527
just want to let them all out.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:55.261
 Yeah!

00:09:58.296 --> 00:10:02.001
[heavy metal music]

